      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add queued webhook support",
        "body": "Related: #100939\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nHigh-volume webhook producers can call OpenClaw thousands of times in a burst, but the current webhook path immediately schedules work without durable backlog visibility, queue-level parallelism controls, or an operator way to pause processing while inspecting the backlog.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds configured webhook queues under `hooks.queues`, a durable SQLite `hook_queue_items` store, queue-backed HTTP ingestion at `POST /hooks/queue/{id}`, per-queue parallelism, default isolated session execution, and shared hook agent dispatch between immediate and queued webhook paths.\n\nIt now also persists queue pause state in SQLite, prevents new queue claims while paused, resumes processing on demand, and keeps already-running queue items isolated from pause/resume toggles.\n\nQueue management is exposed across the intended operator surfaces:\n\n- Gateway RPC: `hooks.queues`, `hooks.queue.items`, `hooks.queue.pause`, `hooks.queue.resume`\n- CLI: `openclaw hooks queue list|items|pause|resume`\n- Agent tool: `hook_queue` with `list`, `items`, `pause`, and `resume`\n- Control UI: queue depth/status counts, paused/running state, pause/resume controls, and recent item inspection in the Automation/Cron page\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can enqueue bursty webhook work, inspect queue depth and queued/running/completed/error items, pause a queue before it claims more work, resume it when ready, and tune concurrency without overwhelming the application. Existing immediate webhook endpoints remain available.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/generate-kysely-types.mjs` - completed\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/hook-queue-store.test.ts src/gateway/server.hooks.test.ts src/gateway/server-request-context.test.ts src/agents/tools/hook-queue-tool.test.ts src/agents/tools/gateway.test.ts src/agents/agent-tools.create-openclaw-coding-tools.test.ts src/agents/agent-tools-agent-config.test.ts src/agents/agent-tools.availability.test.ts src/agents/tool-policy.test.ts src/cli/hooks-cli.test.ts ui/src/lib/cron/index.test.ts ui/src/pages/cron/view.test.ts` - passed, 4 Vitest shards\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/server-request-context.test.ts src/gateway/server.hooks.test.ts src/agents/agent-tools.create-openclaw-coding-tools.test.ts src/agents/tool-policy.test.ts src/agents/tools/hook-queue-tool.test.ts src/agents/tools/gateway.test.ts` - passed after autoreview fix, 3 Vitest shards\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/server.hooks.test.ts src/gateway/server-request-context.test.ts` - passed after startup-order clarification, 1 Vitest shard\n- `pnpm format:check -- ...` on touched source/docs files - passed\n- `pnpm format:docs:check` - passed\n- `pnpm docs:check-mdx` - passed\n- `git diff --check` - passed\n- `pnpm build` - passed after final changes\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local` - final run clean; no accepted/actionable findings\n\nAI-assisted: yes (Codex). Agent transcript logs are not included.\n",
